Subject: [PATCH 07192/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-11: wire SGE into
 the live path -- reachable, selectable, not the default

REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3 through 5699-10 built and thoroughly diagnosed the
SGE mechanism entirely inside scripts/outer_loop_sge_smoke_test.py, an
offline diagnostic harness. arc_llm_strategy_proposer.py was never
imported by arc_competition_agent.py (the live scored-agent
entrypoint) at all -- only by that harness and its own experiment
script. The live agent's real candidate_router has always been
CrossGameDiscriminativeCandidateRouter, a different module (the one
fixed in this session's first bug-fix round, REQ-CAPSTONE-4556-2,
which shipped in the actual 0.12-scoring Kaggle submission).

_load_submitted_candidate_router(game_id) gains
SUBMITTED_SGE_CANDIDATE_ROUTER_ENABLED (default False, matching the
SUBMITTED_COLOR_BLOB_SALIENCE_ENABLED built-but-gated-off precedent).
When enabled, a new _load_sge_candidate_router(game_id) builds
SGECandidateRouter wired to a LocalGGUFProposer configured IDENTICALLY
to the induction proposer's own lazy default (same frozen
Qwen3.5-9B-MTP config, same default port 8919) -- LocalGGUFProposer's
existing port-based server-reuse means this shares ONE warm
llama-server with induction automatically, never a second model load
that would risk the Kaggle 16GB VRAM budget. Falls through to the
discriminative router on any SGE construction failure, never breaking
the live path. game_id is threaded from the constructing policy's
self.short (the real current game), not a placeholder.
SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG gains sge_candidate_router_wired/
sge_candidate_router_enabled for the same audit pattern every other
optional feature follows.

Verified: scripts/arc_orphan_solver_lint.py now passes clean (52
live-closure modules, up from 51) -- SGE is genuinely live-path-
reachable. All 17 tests in test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py pass
(5 new + spec-declaration), including the file's own strict parity
guards (test_shipped_explorer_config_matches_single_source_of_truth,
test_req_capstone_4605_live_stack_integrates_only_non_regression_levers)
proving the DEFAULT live-path behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged.

This is integration, not validation -- the flag stays False. Whether
SGE actually helps on the real live path (induction/frame-change-
scorer/goal-bias all live together, unlike the deliberately-stripped
smoke-test harness) is a separate, not-yet-run experiment: a real
matched-budget A/B on the local submission gate or the live scored
path. Spec: REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-11 with its own scenario.

